        "title": "Cloud Architecture: Models, Patterns, and Trade-offs - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Cloud architecture is the **execution layer** for the entire volume. The consensus protocols from distributed systems and the trust models from security engineering are theoretical until they run on actual infrastructure --- AZs, regions, load balancers, managed services. Cloud architecture answers the question of *where* and *how*: multi-AZ for partition tolerance, managed Kubernetes for consensus (etcd runs Raft), mTLS between services for zero-trust enforcement, health probes for failure detection. Every CAP trade-off, every quorum configuration, every security control from the other two domains materializes here as an infrastructure decision with cost, latency, and blast-radius consequences."
    }
